### ==============================================================
### UserManagement — OData V4 & V2 test scenarios (REST Client)
### ==============================================================
### Start the server first:  npx cds watch
### V4 base: http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/user-management
### V2 base: http://localhost:4004/odata/v2/user-management
###
### AUTH NOTE (verified against a live server):
### The whole service carries @requires: 'Admin' (capitalised). Role
### checks are case-sensitive and the CAP default mocked users
### (alice/bob/carol/...) only carry a lowercase 'admin' role, so
### every request below will 403 until you add a matching mock user.
### Add a project-root `.cdsrc.json` (untracked, dev-only — see chat):
###
### {
###   "requires": { "auth": { "kind": "mocked", "users": {
###     "admin":         { "roles": ["Admin"] },
###     "rohan.sharma":  { "roles": ["Traveller"] }
###   } } }
### }
###
### 'rohan.sharma' (Traveller role, no Admin) is used below to prove
### the service correctly rejects non-admins.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@v4 = {{host}}/odata/v4/user-management
@v2 = {{host}}/odata/v2/user-management

@adminUser = admin
@adminPass = pass
@travellerUser = rohan.sharma
@travellerPass = pass

# Seed data (db/data/burhan.claude-Users.csv / -UserRoles.csv):
# mike.anderson = AGENT only; ravi.kapoor = isLocked true; wei.chen = isLocked true
@userMikeAnderson = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003
@userLauraBennett = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004
@userRaviKapoor = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005
@userWeiChen = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010
@nonExistentUser = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### ==============================================================
### A. Authorization boundary
### ==============================================================

### A1. [V4] Unauthenticated request — expect 401
GET {{v4}}/Users

### A2. [V4] Non-admin (Traveller role) reads Users — expect 403
GET {{v4}}/Users
Authorization: Basic {{travellerUser}} {{travellerPass}}

### A3. [V4] Non-admin calls lockUser — expect 403
GET {{v4}}/lockUser(userId='{{userMikeAnderson}}')
Authorization: Basic {{travellerUser}} {{travellerPass}}

### A4. [V2] Non-admin reads Users — expect 403
GET {{v2}}/Users
Authorization: Basic {{travellerUser}} {{travellerPass}}


### ==============================================================
### B. Users / Roles / UserRoles entities (admin only)
### ==============================================================

### B1. [V4] Admin lists all users
GET {{v4}}/Users
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### B2. [V4] Admin reads one user, expanding role assignments
GET {{v4}}/Users({{userMikeAnderson}})?$expand=roles
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### B3. [V4] Admin lists all role definitions
GET {{v4}}/Roles
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### B4. [V4] Admin lists all user-role assignments, expanding user & role
GET {{v4}}/UserRoles?$expand=user,role
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### B5. [V4] Filter users by isLocked
GET {{v4}}/Users?$filter=isLocked eq true
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### B6. [V2] Admin lists all users
GET {{v2}}/Users
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### B7. [V2] Admin reads one user with $expand
GET {{v2}}/Users(guid'{{userMikeAnderson}}')?$expand=roles
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### B8. [V2] $inlinecount on Roles
GET {{v2}}/Roles?$inlinecount=allpages
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}


### ==============================================================
### C. lockUser / unlockUser — unbound functions
###    V4 call convention: /lockUser(userId='...')  (GET)
###    V2 call convention: /lockUser?userId='...'   (GET)
### ==============================================================

### C1. [V4] Lock an unlocked user — expect true
GET {{v4}}/lockUser(userId='{{userLauraBennett}}')
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C2. [V4] Lock an already-locked user — expect false (no-op, not an error)
GET {{v4}}/lockUser(userId='{{userRaviKapoor}}')
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C3. [V4] Lock a non-existent user — expect 404
GET {{v4}}/lockUser(userId='{{nonExistentUser}}')
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C4. [V4] Unlock a locked user — expect true
GET {{v4}}/unlockUser(userId='{{userWeiChen}}')
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C5. [V4] Unlock an already-unlocked user — expect false
GET {{v4}}/unlockUser(userId='{{userLauraBennett}}')
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C6. [V2] Lock a user via query-string function call
GET {{v2}}/lockUser?userId='{{userLauraBennett}}'
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C7. [V2] Unlock a user via query-string function call
GET {{v2}}/unlockUser?userId='{{userWeiChen}}'
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C8. [V2] Lock a non-existent user — expect 404
GET {{v2}}/lockUser?userId='{{nonExistentUser}}'
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}


### ==============================================================
### D. createUser — action (POST)
### ==============================================================

### D1. [V4] Create user — happy path
# @name createUserV4
POST {{v4}}/createUser
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Nadia",
  "lastName": "Khan",
  "email": "nadia.khan@travelapp.com",
  "roleId": "TRAVELLER"
}

### D2. [V4] Create user — duplicate email (loginName) — expect 409
POST {{v4}}/createUser
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "Anderson",
  "email": "mike.anderson@travelapp.com",
  "roleId": "AGENT"
}

### D3. [V4] Create user — unknown roleId — expect 404
POST {{v4}}/createUser
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Oscar",
  "lastName": "Nolan",
  "email": "oscar.nolan@travelapp.com",
  "roleId": "SUPERUSER"
}

### D4. [V2] Create user — happy path
POST {{v2}}/createUser
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Petra",
  "lastName": "Novak",
  "email": "petra.novak@travelapp.com",
  "roleId": "AGENT"
}


### ==============================================================
### E. resetPassword — action (POST)
### ==============================================================

### E1. [V4] Reset password — empty password — expect 400
POST {{v4}}/resetPassword
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "newPassword": "" }

### E2. [V4] Reset password — too short (< 8 chars) — expect 400
POST {{v4}}/resetPassword
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "newPassword": "short1" }

### E3. [V4] Reset password — non-existent user — expect 404
POST {{v4}}/resetPassword
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{nonExistentUser}}", "newPassword": "ValidPass123" }

### E4. [V4] Reset password — happy path — expect true
POST {{v4}}/resetPassword
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "newPassword": "ValidPass123" }

### E5. [V2] Reset password — happy path
POST {{v2}}/resetPassword
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userLauraBennett}}", "newPassword": "ValidPass456" }


### ==============================================================
### F. assignRole / unassignRole — actions (POST)
### ==============================================================

### F1. [V4] Assign a role the user doesn't have yet — expect true
POST {{v4}}/assignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "roleId": "ADMIN" }

### F2. [V4] Assign the same role again — idempotent, still true, no duplicate row
POST {{v4}}/assignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "roleId": "ADMIN" }

### F3. [V4] Assign role — non-existent user — expect 404
POST {{v4}}/assignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{nonExistentUser}}", "roleId": "ADMIN" }

### F4. [V4] Assign role — unknown roleId — expect 404
POST {{v4}}/assignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "roleId": "SUPERUSER" }

### F5. [V4] Unassign a role the user was never given — expect 404
###      (mike.anderson only ever has AGENT + ADMIN from F1; TRAVELLER was never assigned)
POST {{v4}}/unassignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "roleId": "TRAVELLER" }

### F6. [V4] Unassign an existing role — expect true
POST {{v4}}/unassignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userMikeAnderson}}", "roleId": "ADMIN" }

### F7. [V2] Assign role — happy path
POST {{v2}}/assignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userLauraBennett}}", "roleId": "ADMIN" }

### F8. [V2] Unassign role — happy path
POST {{v2}}/unassignRole
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{userLauraBennett}}", "roleId": "ADMIN" }
